# SWX VFR queue policy: four physical snapshots, two-ready FIFO with oldest-drop, and punctual-recovery credit signal.
# VFR configures four snapshot slots and the display worker keeps a two-frame ready reserve.
# Cold start and resume hold the first ready frame until a second is ready or it has waited one game period.
# On overflow the oldest complete ready frame is canceled and unpinned before the next is promoted.
# A punctual-recovery signal covers an isolated empty refresh in the active regime after priming; the next acquire re-reads depth plus work on the way. Signal-only: both outcomes clear the flag with no pacing effect and no observable difference yet, so the locked cadence is unchanged and the credit counter counts only anticipations effectively used (expected 0 until a pacing use lands).
# Target-rate callbacks use an accumulator against physical display refresh, including non-divisor rates; intentional holds and eligible empty ticks are separate.
# Gate 2 telemetry records ready depth, oldest drops, credits, queue/promote p95 with sample counts, and VFR game/wall window time.
# verify: dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_mtl.m:VFR present queue up to tick
# verify: dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_mtl.m:ready_depth max
# verify: dm/gfx/nvn/hle_nvn.c:window game %.3f s / wall %.3f s
# verify: dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_mtl.m:link_rate = atomic_load(&g_swx_link_hz)
# verify: dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_mtl.m:Signal-only: always 0
# verify: dm/gfx/nvn/hle_nvn.c:Punctual-recovery poll, once per present
